Project 1: Personal Expense Tracker API

What it is. A backend where users sign up, log in, and record their daily expenses with category,
amount, date and note. They can then see monthly totals and spending by category.
Why it impresses. It covers the exact basics every backend interview checks: REST design, CRUD,
database relations, authentication, and validation. It is simple enough to finish in three to four weeks,
which builds your confidence for bigger projects.

Tech stack

Part                                 Use

Language                             Python
Framework                            FastAPI
Database                             SQLite while learning, then PostgreSQL
ORM and migrations                   SQLAlchemy and Alembic
Validation                           Pydantic
Auth                                 Password hashing (passlib or bcrypt) and JWT tokens
Testing                              pytest with FastAPI TestClient

Must have features
• User registration and login with hashed passwords and JWT.
Placement Roadmap for MCA Students 13
• Create, read, update and delete expenses. Each user sees only their own data.
• Categories such as food, travel, rent, shopping.
• Filter expenses by date range and category.
• Summary endpoint: total spent this month and amount per category.
• Proper error messages and status codes (404 when not found, 401 when not logged in).
Extra features once the basics work
• Monthly budget per category with a warning when crossed.
• Export expenses as a CSV file.
• Pagination for the expense list.
• A simple frontend later, even a basic HTML page or Streamlit app calling your API

