How to build it, step by step
1 Write down all the endpoints on paper first, with method, path and what each returns.
2 Design two tables, users and expenses, with a foreign key from expenses to users.
3 Set up the project, virtual environment, and the folder structure above. Push this skeleton to GitHub
on day one.
4 Build the expense CRUD without login first, test everything in the /docs page.
5 Add registration and login, then protect the expense routes so each user only sees their own records.
6 Add filters and the summary endpoint. This is where your SQL GROUP BY knowledge gets used.
7 Write tests for the main routes. Aim for at least ten meaningful tests.
8 Move from SQLite to PostgreSQL and add Alembic migrations.
9 Write the README with endpoint list and screenshots, then deploy.

Deployment

Deploy the API on Render (render.com) or Railway (railway.com) and use a free PostgreSQL database
from a provider such as Supabase (supabase.com) or Neon. Free plans and their limits  change often, so
check the current terms before you choose. Put the live /docs link in your README.
